# Halcora — lite image package set.
#
# Same shell, fewer things in it. For a budget laptop: 4 GB of RAM, two cores,
# integrated graphics, a small SSD.
#
# What is kept, and why: Plasma itself, because the entire design — the Global
# Theme switcher, the HyperOS palette, the window decoration — is Plasma's. A
# lighter desktop would mean throwing away every visual decision this project has
# made, which is a different product rather than a smaller one.
#
# What is dropped: the applications and services that a 4 GB machine cannot
# afford to keep resident, and the ones a minimum install does not need. Each
# removal is a real cost, stated:
#
#   plasma-meta  the whole KDE application suite — replaced by the desktop
#                packages below, which is where most of the saving is
#   discover     no graphical package manager; pacman remains
#   flatpak      no store, so no Flatpak applications
#   firefox      the biggest single application; Epiphany is not included
#                either, so the lite image has no browser until one is installed
#   cups/bluez   printing and Bluetooth are off by default
#
# A user can install any of these afterwards; the point is that the image does
# not pay for them on a machine that cannot run them.

# --- base system ---
base
linux
linux-firmware
mkinitcpio
mkinitcpio-archiso
arch-install-scripts
sudo
nano

# --- filesystems and partitioning ---
btrfs-progs
dosfstools
e2fsprogs
exfatprogs
ntfsprogs
parted
gptfdisk
squashfs-tools

# --- boot ---
grub
efibootmgr
syslinux

# --- networking ---
networkmanager
iwd
wpa_supplicant

# --- audio ---
# PipeWire, not PulseAudio, and without the JACK layer: JACK is for audio work,
# not for a laptop that plays video.
pipewire
pipewire-alsa
pipewire-pulse
wireplumber

# --- desktop, explicitly, instead of plasma-meta ---
# The half-dozen packages that make a working Plasma session, plus the settings
# and display tools. This is the single largest difference between the images.
plasma-desktop
plasma-workspace
kwin
kscreen
systemsettings
plasma-nm
plasma-pa
powerdevil
xdg-desktop-portal-kde
breeze
breeze-icons
sddm
xdg-user-dirs
xdg-utils
konsole
dolphin
kate
ark
udisks2
gvfs

# --- fonts ---
# No emoji set: it is a large package for something a minimum install can live
# without, and Noto's base set already covers text.
noto-fonts
ttf-liberation
inter-font

# --- installer ---
# Our own script, not Calamares. It needs polkit for elevation, konsole for the
# window it runs in, and the base tools already listed above.
polkit
polkit-kde-agent
konsole
